# =============================================================================
#  Cloudflare Pages — custom response headers
#  https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
#  Read by Cloudflare Pages and applied to static-asset responses. The file is
#  never served itself.
#
#  Format:  a URL pattern on its own line, then indented "Name: value" lines.
#  `#` starts a comment. Comments are kept OUTSIDE the blocks on purpose: the
#  documented examples only show them above a block, so a comment sitting
#  between two headers is not something to bet a live site on.
#
#  WHAT THESE HEADERS DO *NOT* DO
#  They cannot block anyone. `_headers` sets metadata only -- a request for
#  /admin.html still returns the file. The only thing that actually refuses to
#  serve it is Cloudflare Access, a separate setting on your account.
#  See ADMIN.md -> "حماية لوحة التحكم".
#
#  This file lives in the project root so a root-folder deploy gets it too, and
#  _tools/deploy.py copies it into _dist/ so there is only ever one copy.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The admin panel: keep it out of search results and out of every cache.
# The page already carries <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">;
# this is the server-side half of the same promise.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/admin.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Cache-Control: no-store


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything else. Header by header:
#
#   X-Frame-Options / frame-ancestors
#       Deny being framed, so nobody can load your site inside theirs and turn a
#       click on the admin panel into something you did not intend.
#   X-Content-Type-Options
#       Stops a browser guessing that a .txt or .md is something else and
#       running it.
#   Referrer-Policy
#       Sends only the origin, never the page path, so a visitor arriving from
#       the admin panel cannot leak your private URL structure.
#   Strict-Transport-Security
#       HTTPS only for the next year. Deliberately WITHOUT includeSubDomains:
#       if you ever attach another subdomain that is not HTTPS-only it would
#       break for anyone who has seen this site before. Add it once every
#       subdomain is covered.
#   Permissions-Policy
#       The site uses none of these features.
#   Content-Security-Policy
#       'unsafe-inline' is needed for script-src and style-src because every
#       page carries a small inline <script> (the WhatsApp/Telegram link
#       filler) and admin.html carries an inline <style> block. Even so it is
#       worth having: it blocks any external script or frame being injected,
#       and pins every third party that is actually allowed.
#
#       The third parties, and why each one is listed:
#         fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com
#             the Cairo + Tajawal fonts
#         www.youtube-nocookie.com
#             the intro video is an iframe on the homepage. Without frame-src
#             it renders as a blank box -- caught in a real browser, not
#             assumed.
#         www.googletagmanager.com + google-analytics.com
#             Google Analytics. It is switched OFF until SITE.gaId is filled
#             in config.js, and is allowed here anyway so that turning it on
#             later needs no edit to this file and breaks nothing.
#
#       api.github.com in connect-src is NOT optional. The admin panel
#       publishes by fetching and PUT-ing the GitHub REST API from the
#       browser, and connect-src 'self' alone blocks that -- the button just
#       says "Failed to fetch" with nothing else wrong. Do not remove it, and
#       do not remove the panel's GitHub publishing without removing this.
#       final_check.py section 10 reads the fetch() calls out of admin.js and
#       fails the build if a host they use is missing from connect-src, so a
#       new integration cannot repeat this.
#
#       data: in img-src is required -- testimonial photos and chat
#       screenshots are stored inline as data URLs inside content.js so they
#       can never 404.
#
#       Adding another embed, font provider or analytics service? Add it here
#       too or it will be blocked. To check, run:
#           python _tools/serve.py --dist --headers
#       then open the page and read the browser console.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.github.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://region1.google-analytics.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
